CM_ SG_ 2566834688 SPNLow "SPN bits 15..0. J1939-73 packs the three most significant bits (SPNHigh) above the FMI, so the whole SPN is SPNHigh * 65536 + SPNLow. Several ECUs send DM1, and the J1939 block reads each one's trouble codes; these signals show whichever arrived last.";
CM_ SG_ 2566834688 SPNHigh "SPN bits 18..16.";
CM_ SG_ 2566834688 ProtectLamp "Whichever ECU's DM1 arrived last. The lamps of the whole bus - the OR of every ECU's - are the system variables j1939.lamp_stop, j1939.lamp_warning, j1939.lamp_mil and j1939.lamp_protect.";
CM_ SG_ 2566799649 LeftTurnSignal "Steady while the stalk is in: the cluster does the flashing.";
CM_ SG_ 2566723361 SeatBeltWarningLamp "1 while the driver's belt is not fastened.";
CM_ SG_ 2566848640 RegimeClass "What the vehicle is doing as the model sees it. RiskLevel is how worried the model is about it, which is a different question.";
CM_ SG_ 2566848640 MessageCounter "Counts 0 to 250: above that a byte means error or not available on a J1939 bus.";

VAL_ 2566848640 RegimeClass 0 "Idle" 1 "Cruise" 2 "HighLoad" 3 "ThermalStress" 4 "Anomaly" ;
VAL_ 2566848640 RiskLevel 0 "Low" 1 "Moderate" 2 "High" 3 "Critical" ;
VAL_ 2566848640 ModelStatus 0 "Waiting" 1 "Running" 2 "Error" 3 "NotAvailable" ;
VAL_ 2566769719 LightingCommand 0 "Off" 1 "Park" 2 "Headlamps" ;
VAL_ 2566769719 TurnSignalSwitch 0 "None" 1 "Left" 2 "Right" ;
CM_ SG_ 2364540160 TransmissionCurrentGear "-1 is reverse, 0 neutral, 1 and up the forward gears. J1939 sends it with an offset of -125, so reverse is 124 on the wire.";
